 "critic": "All cards struck me as probably assembled, though that is a guess about the text, not knowledge of its source. The shortest expose name, occupation, location, and reward slots; the longer ones repeatedly combine an incident, three remedies, and a final explanation for contacting V. Third-person introductions sliding into first person, delivery requests branching into bar shifts, and unfamiliar thieves supposedly proving a conspiracy made those joins conspicuous. Exact duplicates and the many identical Friday-fee appeals reinforced the pattern after rating. Causality worked best when a pressure produced a specific consequence: injury prevents work, or a postponed Claws payment invites escalation. Ivo's deadline and collective stall resistance gave me the strongest pull; generic eviction requests supplied the least reason to care."
